1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,749
The man in charge of keeping McDonald's

2
00:00:01,749 --> 00:00:04,723
Monopoly fair... was the one rigging it.

3
00:00:04,723 --> 00:00:06,476
Jerome Jacobson ran security at the

4
00:00:06,476 --> 00:00:08,591
company that handled the game pieces.

5
00:00:08,591 --> 00:00:10,242
He knew which ones were winners.

6
00:00:10,242 --> 00:00:11,233
So he pulled them out.

7
00:00:11,233 --> 00:00:12,301
And handed them to friends,

8
00:00:12,301 --> 00:00:14,005
family, and people he trusted.

9
00:00:14,005 --> 00:00:15,445
They claimed the prizes.

10
00:00:15,445 --> 00:00:16,768
Again...

11
00:00:16,768 --> 00:00:17,724
and again.

12
00:00:17,724 --> 00:00:19,830
In all, more than twenty million dollars.

13
00:00:19,830 --> 00:00:21,466
Then the FBI found out.

14
00:00:21,466 --> 00:00:22,766
Their plan?

15
00:00:22,766 --> 00:00:24,798
Ask McDonald's to keep the game running.

16
00:00:24,798 --> 00:00:26,156
Agents watched.

17
00:00:26,156 --> 00:00:27,453
And collected evidence.

18
00:00:27,453 --> 00:00:28,393
In 2001,

19
00:00:28,393 --> 00:00:29,713
the arrests began.

20
00:00:29,713 --> 00:00:30,932
Dozens of people pleaded

21
00:00:30,932 --> 00:00:32,954
guilty or were convicted.

22
00:00:32,954 --> 00:00:33,709
Jacobson got about

23
00:00:33,709 --> 00:00:34,938
three years in prison.

24
00:00:34,938 --> 00:00:36,540
The one person who could see the whole

25
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:39,367
game... was the one playing it.
